    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d467">

                <pb facs="0561" n="549" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg549"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.24/1502</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by Mr. Theodore C.
                        Achilles of the Division of European Affairs</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-06-01">June 1, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Bewley called at Mr. Acheson’s request to receive the draft exchange of notes
                    concerning Reverse Lend-Lease from the United Kingdom.</p>
                <p>Mr. Bewley made little comment on the draft but said that he would give a copy to
                    Sir Frederick Phillips who is leaving tonight for London. He noticed the
                    reference in the draft Australian note to “an agreement of May . . ,
                        1942”<anchor n="44" xml:id="d467-f1"/> and said he believed London would <pb
                        facs="0562" n="550" xml:id="pg550"/> still prefer to blanket the Dominions
                    into the United Kingdom agreement. Mr. Acheson explained that any fears London
                    might have that separate agreements with the Dominions would alter the existing
                    procurement procedure were entirely unfounded.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d467-f1" n="44" xml:id="d467-f1-content">
                <p>Whereas the British draft read: “With a view to supplementing Articles II and VI
                    of the Agreement of February 23, 1942 …” the Australian draft substituted “an
                    agreement of May . . , 1942”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
